---
import SimHero from './SimHero.jsx';
import { DEFAULT_CONFIG, MODEL_VERSION, PARAMETER_META, PRESETS } from '../lib/rpni-design/model.mjs';
const groups = [
 {title:'Graft geometry',open:true,keys:['moduleCount','graftLengthMm','graftWidthMm','graftThicknessMm','moduleGapMm'],note:'Each module is a separate free muscle graft. Dimensions describe an idealized rectangular tissue volume; grafts share the selected geometry.'},
 {title:'Recording contacts',open:true,keys:['electrodeSpacingMm','electrodeOffsetMm','electrodeLateralMm','electrodeDepthMm','contactRadiusMm'],note:'One differential channel per graft. Move its two finite disk contacts along the fibers, across the graft, or into its depth.'},
 {title:'Nerve routing & motor units',keys:['nerveDiameterMm','insertionDepthMm','motorUnitsPerModule','routingFidelity','territoryRadiusMm'],note:'Physical graft identity and source command identity remain separate. Routing is a seeded assignment assumption, not a prediction of fascicle identification.'},
 {title:'Regeneration & maturation',keys:['regenerationLagDays','axonSpeedMmDay','nmjMaturationDays','sourceAvailability','observationDay','durationDays'],note:'Arrival uses distance and a prescribed axon speed. Subsequent source maturation is an adjustable exponential. These clocks are not fitted to longitudinal RPNI measurements.'},
 {title:'Electrical source & tissue',keys:['sourceAmplitudeUa','conductionVelocityMps','poleSpacingMm','sourceRadiusMm','sigmaLongitudinalSm','sigmaTransverseSm'],note:'Balanced traveling source tripoles in an infinite, homogeneous anisotropic conductor. Source current is an explicit equivalent-source assumption.'},
 {title:'Drive & acquisition',keys:['targetModule','targetDrive','otherDrive','minFiringHz','maxFiringHz','noiseRmsUv','traceDurationMs','sampleRateHz'],note:'Independent seeded spike trains drive the source pools. Noise is additive, white and Gaussian; there is no fitted amplifier, impedance or movement artifact model.'},
 {title:'Transport diagnostic',keys:['oxygenDiffusivityMm2S','oxygenConsumptionPerS'],note:'Steady, one-dimensional diffusion with first-order consumption and equal supply at both faces. Independent of the electrical source model; it does not predict viability.'},
 {title:'Numerics & reproducibility',keys:['contactOrder','kernelOversampling','seed'],note:'Contact quadrature controls spatial averaging. A common seed helps compare designs without redrawing the synthetic cohort.'},
];
const sweepOptions=[['moduleGapMm','Spacing between grafts'],['electrodeSpacingMm','Bipolar contact spacing'],['electrodeDepthMm','Contact depth'],['electrodeOffsetMm','Contact axial offset'],['contactRadiusMm','Contact radius'],['graftThicknessMm','Graft thickness'],['routingFidelity','Source routing fidelity'],['sigmaTransverseSm','Transverse conductivity'],['observationDay','Recording day']];
---
<div class="rp-lab" data-rpni-lab>
 <SimHero kicker="Neural interface laboratories / Design & testing" title="Regenerative Peripheral Nerve Interfaces" intro="Design the muscle graft. Route the nerve. Position the contacts. Test the signals your assumptions produce." links={[{ href: '/simulations/', label: 'All simulations' }, { href: '/simulations/nerve-regeneration/', label: 'Nerve regeneration' }, { href: '/simulations/rpni-design/methods/', label: 'Model & evidence' }]} />
 <div class="rp-model-note"><span class="rp-badge">Mechanistic design model</span><p>A muscle-graft RPNI forward model with calculated electrical pickup and an independent transport diagnostic. Synthetic motor units; uncalibrated tissue parameters. No clinical outcome, graft-survival or prosthesis-performance prediction.</p></div>
 <section class="rp-presets" aria-label="Design experiments"><span class="rp-section-label">Choose a starting design</span><div>{PRESETS.map(p=><button type="button" data-rp-preset={p.id} aria-pressed="false">{p.label}</button>)}</div></section>
 <div class="rp-workspace">
  <aside class="rp-controls" aria-label="Interface design parameters">
   <header><span class="rp-section-label">01 / Design specification</span><p data-rp="preset-description">A pair of independent muscle-graft interfaces.</p></header>
   {groups.map(group=><details class="rp-control-group" open={group.open}><summary>{group.title}</summary><p class="rp-help">{group.note}</p><div class="rp-control-fields">{group.keys.map(key=>{
    const m=PARAMETER_META[key];return <label><span>{m?.label||key}<small>{m?.unit}</small></span><>{key==='targetModule'?<select data-rp-param={key} aria-label="Target command pool">{[0,1,2,3].map(i=><option value={i} selected={i===DEFAULT_CONFIG[key]}>Pool {i+1}</option>)}</select>:<input type="number" data-rp-param={key} min={m?.min} max={m?.max} step={m?.step??'any'} value={DEFAULT_CONFIG[key]} aria-describedby={`rp-help-${key}`}/>}</><small id={`rp-help-${key}`} class="rp-field-note">{m?.note}</small></label>;
   })}</div></details>)}
   <div class="rp-run-area"><button type="button" class="rp-primary" data-rp="run">Build &amp; test design →</button><button type="button" data-rp="cancel" hidden>Cancel computation</button><p class="rp-dirty" data-rp="dirty" hidden>Design edited · previous results still displayed.</p><p data-rp="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Preparing the reference design…</p><p class="rp-help" data-rp="normalization-note"></p></div>
  </aside>
  <main class="rp-main">
   <section class="rp-scene" aria-label="RPNI anatomical design viewer"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">02 / Geometry review</span><h2>Nerve-to-muscle recording interface</h2></div><span data-rp="geometry-label">Two independent grafts</span></header><div class="rp-viewport" data-rp="viewport"><div class="rp-loading">Preparing anatomical view…</div></div>
    <div class="rp-scene-toolbar"><div class="rp-segment" aria-label="Anatomical view"><button type="button" data-rp-view="longitudinal" aria-pressed="true">Longitudinal</button><button type="button" data-rp-view="transverse" aria-pressed="false">Transverse</button></div><button type="button" data-rp="reset-camera">Reset view</button><label>Inspect contact <select data-rp="contact-select" aria-label="Inspect electrode contact"></select></label></div>
    <details class="rp-display-options"><summary>Anatomy layers &amp; display</summary><div><label><input type="checkbox" data-rp-layer="showNerve" checked/> Nerve routing</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-rp-layer="showTerritories" checked/> Motor-unit territories</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-rp-layer="showElectrodes" checked/> Contacts</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-rp-layer="showLabels" checked/> Labels</label><label><input type="checkbox" data-rp-layer="showOxygen"/> Transport overlay</label></div><p data-rp="renderer-note">Coordinates and ruler in millimeters. Tissue and motor-unit anatomy are procedural.</p></details>
    <p class="rp-contact-detail" data-rp="contact-detail">Select a recording contact to inspect its geometry.</p>
   </section>
   <section class="rp-replay" aria-label="Biological and electrical time"><div><span class="rp-section-label">Biological age / assumed remodeling</span><div class="rp-play-row"><button type="button" data-rp="play-growth">Play growth</button><label class="rp-slider"><span class="rp-sr-only">Days after graft construction</span><input type="range" data-rp="day" min="0" max={DEFAULT_CONFIG.durationDays} step=".25" value={DEFAULT_CONFIG.observationDay}/></label><output data-rp="day-label">Day {DEFAULT_CONFIG.observationDay}</output><button type="button" data-rp="recording-day">Recording day</button></div></div><div><span class="rp-section-label">Electrical replay / recorded at <span data-rp="recorded-day">day {DEFAULT_CONFIG.observationDay}</span></span><div class="rp-play-row"><button type="button" data-rp="play-signal">Play signal</button><label class="rp-slider"><span class="rp-sr-only">Recording time in milliseconds</span><input type="range" data-rp="signal-time" min="0" max={DEFAULT_CONFIG.traceDurationMs} step=".25" value="0"/></label><output data-rp="signal-time-label">0 ms</output><span class="rp-replay-speed">Replay ×0.1</span></div></div><p class="rp-help" data-rp="replay-note">The biological and electrical clocks are separate. Signal replay returns the anatomical view to the recording day.</p></section>
   <div class="rp-metrics">{[['volume','Volume per graft','mm³ / specified geometry'],['arrived','Territories reached','Synthetic axon arrival / shown day'],['maturity','Mean source amplitude gain','Continuous gain / shown day'],['rms','Trace RMS at recording day','µV / signal + noise']].map(([key,label,note])=><div><span>{label}</span><strong data-rp-metric={key}>—</strong><small>{note}</small></div>)}</div>
   <section class="rp-panel rp-recording-panel"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">03 / Calculated electrical recording</span><h2>What the contacts pick up</h2></div><label>Channel <select data-rp="channel-select" aria-label="Selected recording channel"></select></label></header><canvas data-rp="trace-chart" role="img" aria-label="Synthetic bipolar EMG traces in microvolts against time in milliseconds"></canvas><div class="rp-plot-key"><span style="--key:#a47b34">Synthetic signal + noise</span><span style="--key:#2a8d83">Target source contribution</span><span style="--key:#aa5c4a">Other source contribution</span></div><p class="rp-plot-note" data-rp="trace-note">Each channel sums the geometry-dependent motor-unit waveforms and specified noise. These are synthetic extracellular signals, not measured or fitted human EMG.</p><div class="rp-channel-stats" data-rp="channel-stats"></div></section>
   <div class="rp-two-panels">
    <section class="rp-panel"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">04 / Source separation</span><h2>From command pool to channel</h2></div></header><div class="rp-matrix" data-rp="transfer-matrix"></div><p class="rp-plot-note" data-rp="matrix-note">Rows are bipolar channels; columns are source command pools. Values express geometry-dependent pickup under the stated source model.</p><details class="rp-mini-details"><summary>Channel similarity</summary><div class="rp-table-scroll" data-rp="similarity-table"></div><p class="rp-plot-note">Expected clean-channel correlation from shared modeled sources. This is neither finite-trace correlation nor decoder accuracy.</p></details></section>
    <section class="rp-panel"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">05 / Independent transport test</span><h2>Thickness and supply distance</h2></div><span data-rp="oxygen-center">—</span></header><canvas data-rp="oxygen-chart" role="img" aria-label="Steady normalized oxygen concentration across the graft thickness"></canvas><p class="rp-plot-note" data-rp="oxygen-note">Fixed concentration at both faces; first-order consumption. This mathematical slab test does not include a developing vascular network or predict graft survival.</p></section>
   </div>
   <section class="rp-panel rp-growth-panel"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">06 / Assumed biological sequence</span><h2>Arrival precedes source maturation</h2></div><span data-rp="growth-endpoint"></span></header><canvas data-rp="growth-chart" role="img" aria-label="Fraction of synthetic motor units reached and mean source amplitude gain over days"></canvas><div class="rp-plot-key"><span style="--key:#a47b34">Arrival fraction</span><span style="--key:#2a8d83">Mean source amplitude gain</span><span style="--key:#8b8170">Dashed: pinned design</span></div><p class="rp-plot-note">A prescribed nerve-growth delay and speed determine arrival at each synthetic territory. A separate exponential controls subsequent source strength. Oxygen is not used as a hidden viability gate.</p></section>
   <section class="rp-panel rp-sweep-panel"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">07 / Controlled design study</span><h2>Change one design variable</h2></div></header><div class="rp-sweep-controls"><label>Variable<select data-rp="sweep-parameter">{sweepOptions.map(([key,label])=><option value={key}>{label}</option>)}</select></label><label>From<input type="number" data-rp="sweep-low" value="0" step="any"/></label><label>To<input type="number" data-rp="sweep-high" value="30" step="any"/></label><button type="button" data-rp="sweep">Test five values</button></div><label class="rp-output-select">Readout<select data-rp="sweep-metric"><option value="cleanRmsUv">Expected clean RMS / µV</option><option value="otherRmsUv" selected>Expected other-pool RMS / µV</option><option value="targetOtherDb">Target / other power / dB</option><option value="targetFraction">Expected target power fraction</option><option value="oxygenCenterRatio">Hypothetical slab center ratio</option></select></label><canvas data-rp="sweep-chart" role="img" aria-label="Controlled design sweep showing expected off-target source RMS"></canvas><p class="rp-plot-note" data-rp="sweep-note">The same seed, drive and recording horizon are used at each point. Results describe sensitivity to the selected variable within this model.</p><details class="rp-mini-details"><summary>Sweep values &amp; effective geometry</summary><div class="rp-table-scroll" data-rp="sweep-table">Run a study to inspect exact values.</div></details></section>
   <section class="rp-panel rp-ensemble-panel"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">08 / Seed variability</span><h2>Repeat the synthetic population</h2></div><button type="button" data-rp="ensemble">Test eight seeds</button></header><div class="rp-ensemble-results" data-rp="ensemble-results">Run independent seeds at fixed design parameters to see how source placement, current-strength multipliers and command routing change expected signal power.</div><p class="rp-plot-note">Seed variation excludes uncertain biological parameters, patient differences and measurement uncertainty. Its range is not a clinical confidence interval.</p></section>
   <section class="rp-panel rp-compare-panel"><header><div><span class="rp-section-label">09 / Design comparison</span><h2>Keep a reference design</h2></div><div class="rp-action-row"><button type="button" data-rp="pin">Pin current design</button><button type="button" data-rp="clear-reference" disabled>Clear reference</button></div></header><div data-rp="comparison"><p class="rp-plot-note">Pin a result, edit the design and run again. The table will keep the changed assumptions alongside the computed differences.</p></div></section>
   <details class="rp-data-details"><summary>Exact values at the displayed biological age</summary><div class="rp-table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Readout</th><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody data-rp="results-table"></tbody></table></div></details>
   <section class="rp-export-panel"><div><span class="rp-section-label">Reproducible design record</span><p data-rp="manifest">Model {MODEL_VERSION} · seed {DEFAULT_CONFIG.seed} · local computation</p></div><div class="rp-action-row"><button type="button" data-rp="export-json">Experiment JSON</button><button type="button" data-rp="export-traces">Recording CSV</button><button type="button" data-rp="export-growth">Growth CSV</button></div></section>
   <details class="rp-import-panel" data-rp="import-panel"><summary>Restore a saved design</summary><p class="rp-help">Paste an exported experiment or choose its JSON file. Parameters require an exact model-version match; saved numerical results are recomputed.</p><textarea data-rp="import-json" aria-label="Saved experiment JSON" placeholder="Paste the exported experiment JSON here" rows="5" spellcheck="false"></textarea><div class="rp-action-row"><button type="button" data-rp="import-paste">Restore pasted parameters</button><label class="rp-file-button">Choose JSON file<input type="file" data-rp="import-file" accept="application/json,.json"/></label></div></details>
  </main>
 </div>
 <section class="rp-reading"><div><span class="rp-section-label">The interface represented here</span><h2>A nerve-to-muscle recording interface</h2><p>A muscle-graft RPNI supplies a denervated muscle target to a terminal nerve or separated fascicle. Reinnervated muscle can amplify motor commands into recordable electrical activity. This laboratory represents that architecture with separate graft modules, synthetic motor units and physical electrode coordinates.</p><p>A nerve bridge, regenerative sieve, dermal sensory interface and engineered neural graft involve different anatomy and boundary conditions. <a href="/simulations/nerve-regeneration/">Use the nerve-regeneration laboratory</a> to explore repair across a peripheral nerve gap.</p></div><div><span class="rp-section-label">Evidence &amp; verification</span><h2>Inspect every assumption</h2><p>Human and animal studies motivate the design questions. The numerical tests check the equations and limiting cases. The model does not infer patient outcomes, functional muscle force, sensory perception, stimulation thresholds or device safety.</p><p><a href="/simulations/rpni-design/methods/">Read the equations, parameter provenance and primary studies →</a></p><ul data-rp="warnings" class="rp-warnings"></ul></div></section>
 <noscript><p>This design laboratory needs JavaScript for local numerical computation. The <a href="/simulations/rpni-design/methods/">model and evidence</a> remain available without it.</p></noscript>
</div>
<script>
 import { initializeRpniLab } from '../lib/rpni-design/client.mjs';
 initializeRpniLab();
</script>
